  28:     """
  29:     Slide each black border rectangle to the opposite border, recoloring its swept stripe orange and leaving the rectangle black at the far edge.
  30: 
  31:     Input structure
  32:     - The grid contains black rectangular 4-connected masks, each touching exactly one outer border.
  33:     - Grey cells form incidental pattern content; orange is the trail color used when a black mask slides.
  34: 
  35:     Rule
  36:     - Treat all black rectangles as moving simultaneously.
  37:     - A rectangle touching the top or bottom edge moves vertically to the opposite edge in the same columns.
  38:     - A rectangle touching the left or right edge moves horizontally to the opposite edge in the same rows.
  39:     - Recolor the complete swept row or column stripe to orange, then stamp every destination rectangle in black.
  40: 
  41:     Key insight
  42:     - Edge contact gives the slide direction; the output is the set of opposite-edge black rectangles plus their orange trails.
  43:     """
  44:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
  45:     assert g.ndim == 2
